    "b-40-sync-state-within-harnessstate-the-10": {
      "id": "b-40-sync-state-within-harnessstate-the-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Within HarnessState, the sync slot exposes one durable answer for the workflow's current identity, status, progress, blockers, and accepted boundary records. Observation can advance without dispatch authority, while staging mutations require sync to hold the dispatch lease. Canonical cycle and knowledge state change only when the publication projection is committed from validated staging."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-sync-state-the-state-also-preserves-11": {
      "id": "b-40-sync-state-the-state-also-preserves-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The state also preserves enough evidence to choose a safe continuation after interruption. Recovery identifies whether staging survives and where processing resumes; cancellation proves canonical source remained untouched; publication identifies the accepted source and knowledge revisions plus every invalidated dependent identity."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-sync-state-the-sync-workflow-12": {
      "id": "b-40-sync-state-the-sync-workflow-12",
